In `ComparisonTests`, `releaseData()` is called at the end of each test method. If any assertion in the middle of the test fails, `releaseData()` is never reached, leaking the circuit breaker allocation. A `try/finally` (or try-with-resources) pattern would ensure cleanup regardless of test outcome:
```java
public void testRandomDenseDistribution() {
    loadData(() -> random().nextDouble());
    try {
        // ... assertions ...
    } finally {
        releaseData();
    }
}
